{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"PHASE 1 RCA (2026-08-14)\n\nObserved problem: organic Verify run 31846417650 emitted 260 fixture_setup spans >1s totaling 380.393 aggregate worker-seconds. The top five module totals were 103.416 worker-seconds. Fresh serial main baselines confirmed setup, not test-call work, dominates the named fixtures: secret-screen 36 passed/19.99s with ~17s setup; list-filters 17 passed/23.54s with 1.02-2.39s setup each; b636 7 passed/11.37s with 1.29-1.58s setup each; backup 12 passed/14.74s with 0.55-0.98s setup each; inline-push 10 passed/9.64s with 0.42-0.79s setup each.\n\nProven mechanisms and discriminating runtime evidence:\n1. tests/unit/test_secret_screen_e7a9.py:108-120 rebuilds an equivalent virgin store for every consumer. cProfile of two consumers observed two init_repo calls and 99 subprocesses; init_repo consumed 0.919s. A real store built in 0.426s, while three isolated copies took 0.034-0.037s each (~12x); a ticket written in copy A was absent from copy B/template, and identities/worktree refs were disjoint. Secret-screen call behavior cannot explain setup spans.\n2. tests/interfaces/queries/test_list_filters.py:57-90 rebuilds the same 11-ticket/claim/transition/delete/link graph for every test. Two consumers observed 22 create_ticket calls and 192 subprocesses. One population took 1.118s versus 0.126s for two isolated copies (~17.7x per copy); exact IDs/statuses matched, and closing BLK in copy A left copy B/template open. CLI call work is timed separately.\n3. tests/integration/test_concurrency_regression.py:255-283 rebuilds the same bare-remote/A/B/shared-ticket topology for every b636 test. The real topology built in 1.445s versus 0.062s to relocate a complete copy (~23x). Every embedded source path was rewritten, git fsck passed on remote/A/B/both trackers, origin URLs pointed into the copy, linked worktrees were self-contained, object inodes were unshared, the seed was visible, and a copy-only ref did not reach the template. b636 call bodies remain real.\n4. tests/integration/test_prepare_reclaim_backup.py:85-142 rebuilds a fixed branch/tag/blob/bare-remote graph. The real graph built in 0.635s versus 0.046s per copy (~13.8x); all OID relationships and remote snapshot matched, no source path remained, and a copy-only ref did not reach the template. Bundle/verification call work remains real.\n5. tests/interfaces/store/test_inline_write_push.py:32-46 rebuilds a bare origin plus initialized linked-worktree store. The real topology built in 0.487s versus 0.031s per relocated copy (~15.7x); origin/worktree paths were repaired, identity reminted, a real copy write pushed only to the copy origin, and the template origin stayed unchanged.\n\nRoot cause: these function-scoped fixtures execute invariant git/rebar topology construction once per consumer even though the asserted behavior begins after setup. The changeable artifacts are the five fixture scopes/builders above. This is a test-infrastructure defect against the explicit no-coverage-loss runtime goal, not a request to sample or remove coverage. Initialization/recovery contracts remain from-scratch.\n\nOSS/tracker legitimacy: consensus is 3/3. Django 3436cf9 uses setUpTestData plus deep-copy/per-test transaction rollback; Rails 62b5458 loads fixtures once plus per-test rollback/cache invalidation; GitLab dff4132 recommends let_it_be plus rollback/reload and prepared repository bundles, with explicit fallback for migration/delete tests. pytest 68308aa additionally recommends tmp_path_factory session fixtures for expensive generated assets. All were active 2026-08-14; popularity recorded in the investigation (Django 88.4k GitHub stars, Rails 58.7k, GitLab 6.1k stars/12.3k forks). None rejects isolated reuse; each retains from-scratch paths where rollback/copy is not faithful. Closed peculiar-calmy-bubblefish accepted this exact pattern and measured 270.7s -> 186.5s (31%) with nine more tests; adored-duskish-kissingbug strengthened virgin-template assertions. No rejection found.\n\nCaller-dependency gate: expected post-fix behavior is byte/state-equivalent isolated fixture topology with fewer invariant setup subprocesses. All callers are the named tests/fixture consumers. No caller depends on fresh timestamps/UUIDs or shared refs; the experiments preserved recorded OIDs/IDs where contractual and reminted only per-environment identity. Direct initialization/recovery tests are excluded and stay from-scratch. No behavioral dependency blocks Phase 2.\n\nPhase 1 exit: confirmed, cited, parsimonious root cause; all alternatives that assign the measured spans to test bodies or unavoidable fresh topology were rejected. Temporary DEBUG-rebar-debug instrumentation was removed and the worktree returned clean before Phase 2."},"env_id":"0993f6a8-7a6a-4707-a671-c5bbb2691444","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786751807443832001,"uuid":"0cc1e440-f62e-40ea-9c99-40aea33ef3b2"}